{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791390200,"nonce":"mSzpGDEWryormk8cBsrp8N9XE1Y=","title":"Compiler: resolve remaining SOR slowdown across builds with matching native operations","message":"NUC LLVM-off all-kernel comparison of saved baseline 76bc7ca9bb0884e41b4b835e0cfe65dc3bfb707d against the shared dominator plus spill-alignment build (now committed through 9bc3fcd033db1b8a15f0a5d86315fba7be97c5c7) found SOR whole-process medians 11466.982 -\u003e 12390.061 ms (+8.05%). Alignment disabled in the same new executable is 12232.533 ms, so most of the difference is present without the spill-area change. All checksums pass. Other unresolved between-build changes include fannkuch +3.4%, ai/telco about +3%, nqueens +2.6%.\n\nFocused SOR diagnostic runs measured kernel 11148.387 -\u003e 11697.360 ms (~4.9%). Native streams for SOR_execute$s0, its resume2 helper, and adapter match instruction-for-instruction after normalizing host addresses and the expected spill offsets/frame size from the alignment change. Registers, block ordering, call counts and arithmetic operations match. Do not infer an algorithm regression or dismiss the slowdown as noise without isolating host helpers, code placement, call-stack/data layout, and promotion routing. The compiler binary changed; dependency pins and thresholds did not.\n\nRelated: 7312be03da40263e78adbfcbd7a42c6d3afe0a09755d6b005cf7e0cbecfc272f fixed a proven FFT page-split spill penalty, and 7af75d5b3afb72ad19d93bed791987491129d7bddc37bf6121dadfa53079a350 reduced dominator construction. This remaining SOR gap is not resolved by those fixes. The larger boxed-dimension overhead is separately tracked in 64deb1b.\n\nEvidence locally and on NUC: /tmp/zyntax-nuc-spill-all-python-all.json; /tmp/zyntax-spill-{before,after}-sor.trace; /tmp/zyntax-spill-sor-diagnose.log. Local offset-only native diffs /tmp/zyntax-spill-sor-SOR_execute_s0-0.diff and /tmp/zyntax-spill-sor-SOR_execute_s0_resume2-0.diff. Runs used CPUs 0-7 under /tmp/zyntax-nuc-run; original upstream Cranelift bc2f967927f9f0e839095a752bf554c4a09fdd13, no egraph experimental dependency patch.","files":null}]}